@startuml ML Evaluation Framework - Complete Flow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title ML Evaluation Framework - Complete End-to-End Flow

actor User
participant "Training Script\n(train_baseline_time_series.py)" as Train
participant "Golden Dataset\n(JSON file)" as Golden>
participant "Seed Script\n(seed_baseline_test_cases.py)" as Seed
participant "FastAPI\n(/api/v1/*)" as API
participant "CRUD\nOperations" as CRUD
database "PostgreSQL\nDatabase" as DB
participant "run_evaluation.py" as RunEval
participant "EvaluationEngine" as Engine
participant "ModelAdapter\n(BaselineTimeSeriesAdapter)" as Adapter
participant "Model\n(BaselineTimeSeriesModel)" as Model
participant "Evaluator\n(MeanSquaredErrorEvaluator)" as Evaluator
participant "Report Script\n(generate_report.py)" as Report

== Phase 1: Golden Dataset Creation ==
User -> Train: python train_baseline_time_series.py
activate Train

Train -> Train: Load processed_data.csv
Train -> Train: Split train/val/test (70/20/10)
Train -> Train: Create WindowGenerator
Train -> Train: Build Baseline model
Train -> Train: Compile & train model
Train -> Train: Save models/baseline_model.keras
Train -> Train: create_golden_dataset(test_df, 50 samples)

Train -> Golden: Save data/baseline_golden_dataset.json
note right
  JSON structure:
  [
    {
      "case_id": 1,
      "input_data": {"window": [[features...]]},
      "ground_truth": {"prediction": [[temp]]},
      "metadata": {...}
    },
    ...
  ]
end note

Train --> User: ✅ Model trained & golden dataset created
deactivate Train

== Phase 2: Database Seeding ==
User -> Seed: python seed_baseline_test_cases.py
activate Seed

Seed -> Golden: Load golden_dataset.json
Golden --> Seed: List[golden_cases]

loop For each golden_case
    Seed -> API: POST /api/v1/prompts/\n{\n  "test_case_name": "...",\n  "model_type": "baseline_time_series",\n  "input_data": {...},\n  "ground_truth": {...}\n}
    activate API

    API -> CRUD: create_prompt(db, payload)
    activate CRUD

    CRUD -> DB: INSERT INTO test_cases
    activate DB
    DB --> CRUD: TestPrompt(id=N)
    deactivate DB

    CRUD --> API: TestPrompt object
    deactivate CRUD

    API --> Seed: 200 OK {id: N}
    deactivate API
end

Seed --> User: ✅ Created 50 test cases
deactivate Seed

== Phase 3: Model Run Creation ==
User -> API: curl POST /api/v1/runs/\n{\n  "model_name": "baseline_model",\n  "model_version": "1.0",\n  "model_type": "baseline_time_series"\n}
activate API

API -> CRUD: create_model_run(db, payload)
activate CRUD

CRUD -> DB: INSERT INTO model_runs\n(status='pending', total_cases=0)
activate DB
DB --> CRUD: ModelRun(id=R, status='pending')
deactivate DB

CRUD --> API: ModelRun object
deactivate CRUD

API --> User: 200 OK {id: R, status: 'pending'}
deactivate API

== Phase 4: Evaluation Execution ==
User -> RunEval: python run_evaluation.py R
activate RunEval

RunEval -> DB: SELECT * FROM model_runs WHERE id=R
activate DB
DB --> RunEval: ModelRun(id=R, model_type='baseline_time_series')
deactivate DB

RunEval -> RunEval: Load models/baseline_model.keras
RunEval -> Model: new BaselineTimeSeriesModel(model_path)
activate Model
Model --> RunEval: model instance
deactivate Model

RunEval -> Adapter: new BaselineTimeSeriesAdapter(model)
activate Adapter
Adapter --> RunEval: adapter instance
deactivate Adapter

RunEval -> Evaluator: new MeanSquaredErrorEvaluator()
activate Evaluator
Evaluator --> RunEval: evaluator instance
deactivate Evaluator

RunEval -> Engine: new EvaluationEngine(db, adapter, evaluator)
activate Engine

RunEval -> Engine: run_evaluation(run_id=R)

Engine -> DB: UPDATE model_runs SET status='running' WHERE id=R
activate DB
deactivate DB

Engine -> DB: SELECT * FROM test_cases\nWHERE model_type='baseline_time_series'
activate DB
DB --> Engine: List[TestPrompt] (50 cases)
deactivate DB

loop For each TestPrompt
    Engine -> Adapter: run(prompt.input_data)
    activate Adapter

    Adapter -> Model: predict(input_data)
    activate Model

    Model -> Model: _preprocess_input(input_data)
    note right: Convert to numpy array\nEnsure shape (batch, timesteps, features)

    Model -> Model: self.model.predict(preprocessed)

    Model --> Adapter: {"prediction": [[value]], "metadata": {...}}
    deactivate Model

    Adapter --> Engine: model_output
    deactivate Adapter

    Engine -> CRUD: create_response(db, run_id=R,\ntest_case_id=prompt.id, output_data=model_output)
    activate CRUD

    CRUD -> DB: INSERT INTO responses
    activate DB
    DB --> CRUD: Response(id=N)
    deactivate DB

    CRUD --> Engine: response
    deactivate CRUD

    Engine -> Evaluator: evaluate(expected=prompt.ground_truth,\nactual=response.output_data)
    activate Evaluator

    Evaluator -> Evaluator: _extract_predictions(actual)
    Evaluator -> Evaluator: _extract_ground_truth(expected)
    Evaluator -> Evaluator: Calculate MSE, MAE, RMSE
    Evaluator -> Evaluator: Calculate normalized score

    Evaluator --> Engine: EvaluationResult(\n  score=0.95,\n  passed=True,\n  metrics={mse, mae, rmse},\n  feedback="..."\n)
    deactivate Evaluator

    Engine -> CRUD: create_evaluation(db, response_id=N,\nevaluator_type="MeanSquaredErrorEvaluator",\nscore, passed, metrics, feedback)
    activate CRUD

    CRUD -> DB: INSERT INTO evaluations
    activate DB
    DB --> CRUD: Evaluation(id=E)
    deactivate DB

    CRUD --> Engine: evaluation
    deactivate CRUD

    Engine -> DB: UPDATE model_runs\nSET completed_cases=completed_cases+1
    activate DB
    deactivate DB
end

Engine -> CRUD: complete_model_run(db, run_id=R)
activate CRUD

CRUD -> DB: UPDATE model_runs\nSET status='completed', completed_at=NOW()
activate DB
DB --> CRUD: ModelRun(status='completed')
deactivate DB

CRUD --> Engine: completed_run
deactivate CRUD

Engine --> RunEval: ModelRun(status='completed')
deactivate Engine

RunEval --> User: ✅ Evaluation complete\nTotal: 50, Completed: 50, Failed: 0
deactivate RunEval

== Phase 5: Report Generation ==
User -> Report: python generate_report.py R
activate Report

Report -> DB: SELECT e.*, r.*, t.*\nFROM evaluations e\nJOIN responses r ON e.response_id=r.id\nJOIN test_cases t ON r.test_case_id=t.id\nWHERE r.run_id=R
activate DB
DB --> Report: List[evaluation, response, test_case]
deactivate DB

Report -> Report: Calculate aggregates:\n- overall_accuracy\n- mean MSE, MAE, RMSE\n- score statistics\n- best/worst predictions

Report -> Report: save_performance_charts(\n  mse_distribution,\n  mae_distribution,\n  score_distribution,\n  metrics_over_time\n)

Report -> Report: Save reports/run_R_time_series_report.png

Report --> User: ✅ Report generated\nMean MSE: 0.0142\nMean MAE: 0.0852\nCharts saved to reports/
deactivate Report

@enduml
